{% from "macros.njk" import callout, snippet with context %}

{% set design %}
<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-usage">Usage</h2>
  <p>Buttons trigger actions — never navigation between destinations (that is
     what the shells' tabs and nav rows are for). The three variants encode
     emphasis: one filled (primary) action per view, outline for important
     secondary actions, text for everything else.</p>
  <h3>Do use it when</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>There is <strong>one clear primary action</strong> in view — give it
        <code>fl-btn--filled</code> and everything else less weight.</li>
    <li>The action sits inside a card, dialog content, or a form's action row
        (secondary link left, filled button right — the auth-card pattern).</li>
    <li>Actions are toolbars of equals (Compose / Snooze / Archive) — use
        text buttons so nothing competes with the content.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Don't use it when</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The element navigates to another destination — use a real link or a
        nav item; buttons that navigate confuse keyboard and screen-reader
        users.</li>
    <li>You need icon-only actions in chrome (top bars, list rows) — that is
        <code>fl-icon-btn</code>, not a text button.</li>
    <li>More than one filled button would appear in the same view — two
        primaries cancel each other out.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-anatomy">Anatomy</h2>
  <div class="docs-anatomy">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 600 300" role="img" aria-label="Button anatomy diagram">
      <!-- Filled button -->
      <rect x="1" y="1" width="598" height="99" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#dadce0"/>
      <rect x="40" y="31" width="120" height="40" rx="4" fill="#1a73e8"/>
      <rect x="72" y="47" width="56" height="8" rx="4" fill="#ffffff"/>
      <!-- Outline button -->
      <rect x="1" y="100" width="598" height="99" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#dadce0"/>
      <rect x="40" y="130" width="120" height="40" rx="4" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#dadce0"/>
      <rect x="72" y="146" width="56" height="8" rx="4" fill="#1a73e8"/>
      <!-- Text button -->
      <rect x="1" y="199" width="598" height="99" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#dadce0"/>
      <rect x="40" y="229" width="120" height="40" rx="4" fill="#ffffff"/>
      <rect x="72" y="245" width="56" height="8" rx="4" fill="#1a73e8"/>
      <!-- keyline markers -->
      <line x1="40" y1="31" x2="160" y2="31" stroke="#1a73e8" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
      <line x1="40" y1="71" x2="160" y2="71" stroke="#1a73e8" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
      <!-- callout numbers -->
      <g font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="700">
        <g><circle cx="28" cy="25" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="28" y="29" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">1</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="180" cy="51" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="180" y="55" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">2</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="28" cy="124" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="28" y="128" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">3</text></g>
        <g><circle cx="28" cy="223" r="11" fill="#1a73e8"/><text x="28" y="227" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">4</text></g>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>40px height</strong> — M2 touch-target size at every breakpoint; inline-flex centers the label.</li>
      <li><strong>Filled</strong> — solid accent fill, surface-colored label; hover/active darken via the accent-hover/pressed tokens (a state layer without transparency).</li>
      <li><strong>Outline</strong> — 1px border, accent label, hover takes the flat <code>--fl-hover</code> fill.</li>
      <li><strong>Text</strong> — accent label, no fill until hover.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-behavior">Behavior</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>State layers are fills, not shadows or ripples:</strong> filled darkens on hover and further on press; outline and text take the <code>--fl-hover</code> gray on hover. Transitions run at <code>--fl-dur</code>/<code>--fl-ease</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Variants combine with icons:</strong> put a <code>fl-icon</code> placeholder (or a real SVG) inside with 8px margin — the flex layout centers it. Icon sizes are not auto-adjusted inside <code>fl-btn</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Adjacent pairs:</strong> the convention is text button left, filled right (Cancel / Confirm), right-aligned with an 8px gap — mirrors the auth-card action row.</li>
    <li><strong>Buttons are <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;a&gt;</code></strong> — both get the styles; anchors should still only be used where the action really is a navigation-adjacent verb ("Create account").</li>
    <li><strong>Disabled state is not styled in 0.1</strong> — the browser dims nothing here. Interim: <code>[disabled]</code> blocks clicks but keeps full color; add <code>style="opacity:.38"</code> or your own rule. Logged as a docs-driven requirement.</li>
    <li><strong>Related controls:</strong> <code>fl-icon-btn</code> (40px rounded-square, for chrome) and <code>fl-fab</code> (56px fixed circle docked above the tab bar) — see the bottom-nav shell page.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Buttons are real <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> elements — Enter/Space activation, form submission, and focus are platform behavior; nothing is reimplemented.</li>
    <li>Labels are visible text; don't ship icon-only text buttons — if there is no room for text, <code>fl-icon-btn</code> + <code>aria-label</code> is the pattern.</li>
    <li><code>:focus-visible</code> gets the 2px accent ring globally (on the accent-filled button the ring still reads via its offset).</li>
    <li>State is conveyed by color only in hover/press — which is fine, because those states are pointer-specific; the *enabled/disabled* distinction must not be color-only, so don't rely on the (unstyled) disabled state alone — disable the attribute <em>and</em> add an opacity or text change.</li>
    <li>Buttons that toggle (e.g. "Follow"/"Following") should carry <code>aria-pressed</code>.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
{% endset %}

